{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. You were brought in because your heart was racing. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I was at dinner and people said I looked bad. My heart was pounding, like it was going to jump out of my chest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve had this before, right? Atrial fibrillation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, a few times. They said it’s from drinking. But I just forgot my meds after the last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Your heart rate was over 130 when you came in. We gave you diltiazem to slow it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why I feel better now? It’s not racing as much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your rate is down to 98 now, still irregular, but much safer. We’ll keep you on that and add metoprolol to help control it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been drinking a lot since I got out. Like, a whole gallon of vodka."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely what triggered this episode. Alcohol can really stress your heart, especially with your history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know, I know. But I keep forgetting my pills. And I didn’t even pick them up last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to help you with that. For now, we’re giving you thiamine, folic acid, and vitamins. You need that after heavy drinking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why I’ve been feeling so off? Not just the heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly. Alcohol depletes important nutrients. We’re also watching for withdrawal, so we’ll give you some diazepam if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to go through withdrawal again. It’s awful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2115-04-27 19:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you comfortable. You’re already on the CIWA protocol, and so far, you’re not showing signs of withdrawal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2115-04-27 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood work came back. No signs of a heart attack — troponins are negative. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2115-04-27 20:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Wait, could it have been a heart attack?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2115-04-27 20:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your symptoms and EKG didn’t suggest one, and the labs confirm it. Your chest pain is likely from muscle tenderness or stomach irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2115-04-27 20:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had pain in my belly too, near the top right."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2115-04-27 20:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your liver enzymes and lipase. Everything’s normal. It’s probably irritation from alcohol — gastritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2115-04-27 20:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So nothing’s damaged?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2115-04-27 20:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No acute damage, but long-term drinking can harm your liver and heart. That’s why cutting back is so important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2115-04-27 23:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2115-04-27 23:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Heart’s not racing. Still a little shaky, but not bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2115-04-27 23:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Your heart rate’s 88, still in afib but well-controlled. We’ll keep you on the diltiazem and metoprolol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2115-04-27 23:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Are those the same meds I was on before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2115-04-27 23:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re adjusting them. You’ll take diltiazem once daily and metoprolol three times a day now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2115-04-27 23:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Three times? I’m going to forget."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2115-04-27 23:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you a pill organizer. And we’re adding Campral — it helps reduce alcohol cravings."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2115-04-27 23:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That might help. I want to stop, really. It’s just hard."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2115-04-27 23:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to support you. You mentioned you’re going to the beach — will you have access to care there?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2115-04-27 23:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, there’s a clinic. And I’ll go to a program they have for alcohol treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2115-04-27 23:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’ll send your records there if you’d like."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2115-04-28 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your repeat labs look good. Liver tests are stable, no signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2115-04-28 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2115-04-28 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still in atrial fibrillation, but rate is under 100. That’s what we want. We’ll keep you on the meds and monitor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2115-04-28 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No more IV stuff?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2115-04-28 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, you’re doing well on oral meds. We’ll remove the IV lines soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2115-04-28 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning if all stays stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2115-04-28 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Already? I feel okay, but I don’t want to end up back here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2115-04-28 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The biggest risk is going back to drinking and missing meds. That’s what keeps bringing you in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2115-04-28 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. I’m going to try this time. The program might help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2115-04-28 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re adding Campral and keeping your vitamins. Take them every day — they protect your body."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2115-04-28 14:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the heart pills?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2115-04-28 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Diltiazem once a day, metoprolol three times, aspirin daily. We’re simplifying from your last discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2115-04-28 14:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll do my best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2115-04-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. Your heart rate is 92, you’re alert, and labs are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2115-04-29 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No more tests?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2115-04-29 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray was clear, no pneumonia or fluid. EKG showed no strain. You’re good to go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2115-04-29 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ll try to stick with the plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2115-04-29 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re counting on it. If you don’t cut down on alcohol, this could become life-threatening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2115-04-29 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hear you. I don’t want to keep doing this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2115-04-29 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re going home with all your meds — 30-day supply. Call your clinic if you need help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2115-04-29 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll go to that program."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2115-04-29 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Take care of yourself. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2115-04-29 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doc. I’ll do better."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2115-04-27 19:28:00",
    "admission_end": "2115-04-29 11:04:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "John, a man with a history of hypertension and alcohol use disorder, was admitted after a heavy drinking episode involving a gallon of vodka, presenting with atrial fibrillation with rapid ventricular response. He reported forgetting and not picking up his medications after a recent discharge. On admission, his heart rate was elevated at 130s, and he was treated with IV and oral diltiazem, followed by the addition of metoprolol to achieve rate control under 100. His chest pain was attributed to chest wall tenderness and gastritis, with normal cardiac enzymes and a clear chest X-ray. He received diazepam per CIWA protocol for alcohol withdrawal prevention, along with thiamine, folic acid, and multivitamins. Abdominal pain resolved with supportive care. By discharge, he was stable, alert, and ambulatory, with a simplified medication regimen including Campral to support alcohol cessation. He planned to engage in outpatient treatment and was discharged home with follow-up instructions.",
    "problems": [
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Alcohol withdrawal",
      "Alcohol abuse, unspecified",
      "Other chest pain",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Lack of housing",
      "Personal history of noncompliance with medical treatment, presenting hazards to health"
    ]
  }
}
